// `panic` ends the program on purpose. The message is the program's, so it goes to
// stderr with the "panic:" prefix and the process exits with 70 - the same code
// the runtime uses for an unrecoverable error, which is what makes a panic
// indistinguishable from one at the exit-code level on purpose.
int function main() {
    print("before the panic");
    panic("deliberate stop");
    print("never reached");
    return 0;
}
